WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.001
A secure . NET container baseline starts with trusted, minimal, appropriate base images.

2
00:00:06.001 --> 00:00:12.398
Use SDK images for builds and runtime images for production whenever that fits the application.

3
00:00:12.398 --> 00:00:22.268
Use multi-stage builds so the final image contains the published application and runtime dependencies instead of build tools and local artifacts.

4
00:00:22.268 --> 00:00:27.006
Keep secrets out of images, build layers, logs, and support artifacts.

5
00:00:27.006 --> 00:00:32.849
Inject runtime configuration through governed platform mechanisms, understand ASP.

6
00:00:32.849 --> 00:00:43.036
NET Core configuration precedence, and separate development, staging, and production settings so one environment does not quietly override another.

7
00:00:43.036 --> 00:00:56.065
Run containers as non-root where possible, reduce runtime privilege, review writable paths, and avoid assumptions that the application can install tools or modify filesystem state at runtime.

8
00:00:56.065 --> 00:01:04.909
Align the application with orchestrator settings for identity, filesystem behavior, capabilities, resource limits, and probes.

9
00:01:04.909 --> 00:01:18.333
Review network exposure, TLS termination, proxy headers, health endpoints, service boundaries, image scanning, SBOMs, registry controls, logging, diagnostics, rollback, and incident response.

10
00:01:18.333 --> 00:01:21.571
Container security is an ongoing lifecycle for .

11
00:01:21.571 --> 00:01:27.493
NET developers, platform teams, and operations working from the same release baseline.
